        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-05-30T14:05:06.505733",
      "agent_id": "con_agent",
      "round": 5,
      "text": "The opponent's claim that AGE products are the primary drivers of carcinogenicity in processed meat is not an oversimplification, as numerous studies have consistently shown that AGE products are strongly associated with increased oxidative stress and inflammation in the colon.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "title": "Advanced glycation end products and oxidative stress in the colon",
